  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">ICTJ Uganda program 2022-2027: Supporting inclusive and citizen-driven transitional justice processes in Uganda.</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Supporting inclusive, and citizen-driven transitional justice processes in Uganda.  

This program contributes to the following outcomes: 


Outcome 1: Civil society organizations and victims&#x2019; groups are equipped with the capacity and technical tools to play a meaningful role in advancing truth, justice, and reparations for victims

Outcome 2: State-led transitional justice processes are inclusive and effectively address the justice demands of victims in accordance with international human rights standards and best practices.</narrative>
  </description>
